      "content": "It's easy to lose faith when things seem pointless and overwhelming. Existential crises can be particularly daunting when our place in the world feels uncertain and our efforts seem futile. However, the darkness you've described can also be a deeply human, and ordinary experience to which many have responded with courage, resilience, and a determination to find meaning despite the void.",
      "source": "target",
